-- title:
--   Reduced-norm classes and functions factoring through the reduced norm
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $F=\mathbb Q(\sqrt{17})$ with ring of integers $\mathcal O_F$, $D=\left(\frac{-1,-3}{F}\right)$ is the fixed totally definite quaternion algebra, $\mathcal O\subset D$ is the fixed maximal order of equation (3.7), and $Q=(2,\omega)$, $\omega=\frac{1+\sqrt{17}}2$, is the fixed prime ideal above $2$.
--
--   For a full $\mathcal O_F$-lattice $I\subset D$ write $\operatorname{nrd}(I)\subset F$ for the $\mathcal O_F$-submodule generated by the reduced norms $\operatorname{nrd}(x)$, $x\in I$. This file adds two notions.
--
--   1. **Reduced-norm classes.** Two lattices $I,J\subset D$ are *norm-class equivalent* if there is a totally positive $x\in F$ (positive under both real embeddings) with
--   $$\operatorname{nrd}(J)=x\,\operatorname{nrd}(I).$$
--   For locally principal right ideals this says that $\operatorname{nrd}(I)$ and $\operatorname{nrd}(J)$ define the same element of the narrow class group $\mathrm{Cl}^+(F)$.
--
--   2. **Functions factoring through the reduced norm.** Let $A\subset D$ be an order and $h$ a complex function on ideal classes. Then $h$ *factors through the reduced norm on* $\mathrm{Cl}(A)$ if
--   $$h([I])=h([J])$$
--   for all locally principal right $A$-ideals $I,J$ that are norm-class equivalent, i.e. if the restriction of $h$ to $\mathrm{Cl}(A)$ is the pull-back of a function on $\mathrm{Cl}^+(F)$ along $[I]\mapsto[\operatorname{nrd}(I)]$.
--
--   These functions are the linear span of the norm-character functions $[g]\mapsto\chi(\operatorname{nrd}(g))$ of the paper, which form the non-cuspidal (Eisenstein) part of the Brandt module $M=\{h:\mathrm{Cl}(A)\to\mathbb C\}$; its complement is the part that the Jacquet–Langlands correspondence sends to Hilbert cusp forms. The definition lets the Ramanujan–Petersson bound for the Hecke operator be stated without an inner product.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: one-dimensional constituents given by norm characters $h([g])=\chi((\operatorname{nrd}(g_R))_R)$ of the idele double coset space → functions of the class of a right ideal that depend only on the narrow class of its reduced norm; reason: the mission's class set is written with right ideals $I=D\cap g\hat A$, for which $\operatorname{nrd}(I)$ is the ideal of the idele $\operatorname{nrd}(g)$; a character of $\hat F^\times$ trivial on $\operatorname{nrd}(\hat A^\times)=\hat{\mathcal O}_F^\times$ and on $\operatorname{nrd}(D^\times)=F^\times_+$ is a character of $\mathrm{Cl}^+(F)$, and such characters span the functions on $\mathrm{Cl}^+(F)$
--   - encoding: functions on the class set → functions on the ambient quotient of all subsets of $D$, constrained only on classes of locally principal right $A$-ideals; reason: this is the convention of the shared ideal-class definitions
--
--   **Formalization Note** `normClassEquivalent I J` is $\exists x$ totally positive with `idealNorm J = principalIdeal x * idealNorm I` (product of $\mathcal O_F$-submodules of $F$); `factorsThroughNorm A h` quantifies over all `I J` with `locallyPrincipal A I`, `locallyPrincipal A J`.
-- source:
--   Olga Kharlampovich, Igor Pak, Alina Vdovina, STOC 2027 submission #136 (October 2026), source.pdf SHA-256 27d691a82d8af863e511e7e6b00cee95779d914645846d2974f876836db8f83b, p.19 (PDF p.20), proof of Proposition 5.1, second paragraph (norm-character functions h([g]) = χ((nrd(g_R))_R)); see also L. Dembélé and J. Voight, Explicit methods for Hilbert modular forms (2013), Definition 3.7. https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-1/136.pdf

import Definitions.Def_RamanujanLiftTower136_Tower_Ideals

namespace RamanujanLiftTower136.Tower

/-- Two lattices have reduced norms in the same narrow ideal class of `F`:
`nrd(J) = x · nrd(I)` for a totally positive `x ∈ F`. -/
def normClassEquivalent (I J : Set D) : Prop :=
  ∃ x : F, totallyPositive x ∧ idealNorm J = principalIdeal x * idealNorm I

/-- A function on ideal classes factors through the reduced norm on the class set of `A`:
its value at the class of a locally principal right `A`-ideal depends only on the narrow
ideal class of the reduced norm of that ideal. -/
def factorsThroughNorm (A : Set D) (h : IdealClass → ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∀ I J : Set D, locallyPrincipal A I → locallyPrincipal A J →
    normClassEquivalent I J → h (idealClass I) = h (idealClass J)

end RamanujanLiftTower136.Tower


